# Conventional Commits — Required

RULE: ALL commit messages MUST use conventional commit format. This is the ONLY way auto version bumping on main merge works.
WHY: GitHub Action reads the squash-merge commit prefix to determine semver bump type. Free-form messages produce no bump → Cloud Build idempotent conflict on next build.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/feature-branch-workflow.md

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

BREAKING CHANGE: <description>  # in footer, triggers major bump
```

## Types and Version Bumps

| Type | Bump | When to use |
|------|------|-------------|
| `feat:` | minor | New feature, new API, new behaviour |
| `fix:` | patch | Bug fix, incorrect behaviour corrected |
| `BREAKING CHANGE:` | major | API removed/changed incompatibly (in footer or `feat!:`) |
| `chore:` | none | Tooling, config, non-code changes |
| `docs:` | none | Documentation only |
| `refactor:` | none | Code restructure, no behaviour change |
| `test:` | none | Tests only |
| `ci:` | none | CI/CD pipeline changes |

## DO

```bash
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat: add ConfigReloader to UTS"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "fix: correct tier boundary in path-dependency-ci rule"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "chore: update .gitignore"
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "feat!: remove ConfigStore from UCI (BREAKING CHANGE: import from UTS)"
```

## NEVER

```bash
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "update stuff"          # no type prefix → no version bump
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "wip"                   # not conventional
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "fixed the thing"       # not conventional
bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "bump version to 1.3.0" # NEVER bump locally — CI does this on merge
```

## Local Version Bumping

NEVER bump version in pyproject.toml or package.json locally on a branch.
The GitHub Action bumps version automatically on merge to main, based on the commit message type.
Manual bumps on branches create double-bumps (branch bump + CI bump = skipped semver).

## Scope (optional but encouraged)

Scope identifies which component changed:
- `feat(ConfigReloader): extract from UCI to UTS`
- `fix(quality-gates): remove git reset --hard suggestion from Option 1`
- `chore(quickmerge): add --no-pr flag`

## Enforcement

- commit-msg hook (pre-commit): validates format before commit is created
- quickmerge.sh Stage 0: validates COMMIT_MSG format, exits 1 if not conventional
- GitHub Actions version-bump.yml: reads type prefix from squash-merge commit

## Breaking Changes in Internal Libraries/Services

When a library or service makes a breaking API change that forces consumers to update their code,
use `feat!:` (bang) or include `BREAKING CHANGE:` in the commit footer. This triggers a **major**
version bump (e.g. `1.4.2` → `2.0.0`) in the CI.

Consumers of that library MUST then update their `pyproject.toml` version constraint and fix
call sites before their next merge to main.

See full protocol: `cursor-rules/dependencies/breaking-change-major-version-protocol.mdc`
